package localui

import (
	"net/http"
)

type capabilityStatus string

const (
	capabilityGreen  capabilityStatus = "green"
	capabilityYellow capabilityStatus = "yellow"
	capabilityRed    capabilityStatus = "red"
)

type capability struct {
	Title, Detail string
}

type capabilityGroup struct {
	Title, Summary string
	Status         capabilityStatus
	Items          []capability
}

// Keep this teacher-facing snapshot aligned with docs/engine-capabilities.md.
// Recorded live evidence and local checks are different kinds of verification.
const capabilitiesReviewed = "2026-10-21"

var capabilityGroups = []capabilityGroup{
	{
		Title: "Working with recorded evidence", Status: capabilityGreen,
		Summary: "The tools below have recorded checks within each feature's stated scope. These checks do not establish every client or student workflow.",
		Items: []capability{
			{"Discover teacher courses and read modules", "Verified in Canvas Live."},
			{"Collaborative group sets, clubs, and Pages", "CS8 Canvas Live, 2026-10-17: group-set/club create/read/pull/update, membership add/move/remove, and a member-editable group Page create/pull/edit/unpublish/history. Local checks also cover collaborative-only scope, stable references, pending requests, no replay and body conflict preservation. Local fixes reviewed 2026-10-19 preserve unrelated group-set settings and explicit clears. Self sign-up/allocation and student access/editor behavior remain unobserved."},
			{"Git-managed install (release tooling and Engine support)", "Added in Dev, 2026-10-21, local tests and a throwaway-repo trial only: a clone of the userinstall branch gets its playbooks and AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md from git, and get-engine.cmd downloads and checksum-verifies the Engine. In a git install the Engine reports install_kind and whether it matches the manifest, playbooks update/status/replace change nothing, and UserSync carries only context/ and Teacher_Override.md. Released 2026-10-21 as v1.1.0-beta.2 (release build): on the developer's home PC a fresh clone of the published userinstall branch ran get-engine.cmd, downloaded cse.exe and the extension from the GitHub release with matching checksums, reported install_kind git and engine_matches_manifest true, and left git status clean. On 2026-10-21 the home PC's existing sync-mode UserInstall was migrated in place (git init, checkout of origin/userinstall, get-engine.cmd): release Engine with install_kind git and a matching manifest, rules still read from the OneDrive UserSync folder, saved courses listed through MCP, git status clean. Pending: a district PC and the background stage-and-apply update flow."},
			{"Individual assignments for selected book clubs", "Added in Dev, reviewed 2026-10-19: prepare-audience records a dated union of active student enrollments with accepted memberships in selected collaborative clubs. Assignment creation and initial assignment-dates application use student overrides with independent submissions, preserve manual exceptions, and hold empty, incomplete or changed snapshots before publication. Review shows the source, stable refs and preserved access. Accepted and uncertain writes are retained without replay. Focused synthetic checks only; Canvas Live direct access, shared-module and student views remain pending. Explicit refresh now prepares a separate assignment-dates action with additions/removals/retained students, exact owned rows, current/history work protection and safe partial changes. Original create receipts and later teacher edits are preserved; no-op and unfinished baselines are checked. Course Pages and New Quizzes carry the same intent through their own entries below."},
			{"Course Pages for selected book clubs", "Added in Dev, reviewed 2026-10-19: a course Page can carry the same individual club audience. Push creates it unpublished, applies the complete date-details restriction, finishes requested module placement and publishes last; a refused or uncertain audience never publishes. Unrelated override rows and availability dates survive the collection replacement, Canvas 204 is accepted, and an audience-only update sends no stale body. Explicit refresh recomputes the managed student row while preserving manual rows and newer teacher edits; Pages have no submission evidence route, so removals are not work-protected. Focused synthetic checks only; Canvas Live direct access, shared-module and student views remain pending."},
			{"New Quizzes for selected book clubs", "Added in Dev, reviewed 2026-10-19: a QuizForge file can carry the same individual club audience. The restriction targets the quiz's exact associated assignment, so the quiz stays one gradebook column and each student answers independently; a quiz whose assignment is native group work is refused. Push creates the quiz, adds items, applies settings and module placement, applies the audience and publishes last, so a refused or uncertain audience never publishes. The sidecar records accepted stages and a resume repeats only unfinished work; a sidecar bound to another Canvas or course is refused, and older sidecars keep working. Audience-only refresh returns an assignment-dates action and sends no quiz, item or settings write, while New Quiz attempts and grades protect removals. Focused synthetic checks only; Canvas Live club-audience quiz and student views remain pending."},
			{"A whole club unit in one shared module", "Added in Dev, reviewed 2026-10-19: one club audience can produce a course Page, an individual assignment and a New Quiz, each prepared, reviewed and pushed on its own so a held resource never blocks the others. Each resource is created unpublished, restricted to the selected clubs, placed in the requested existing module and published last. The module is a navigation list and carries no audience; each child keeps its own restriction, and an existing module keeps its unrelated entries while gaining one native entry per resource in the requested order. Membership refresh is per resource: assignment and quiz removals are work-protected, Page removals are not. Focused synthetic checks only; Canvas Live module-list, direct-access and student views remain pending."},

			{"Create assignments with directions, points, dates, and submission settings", "Creation and edits verified in Canvas Live."},
			{"Publish assignments when requested", "Verified in Canvas Live. New assignments wait for requested rubric and module pieces to succeed before publication."},
			{"Edit existing assignments while preserving unrelated content", "Verified in Canvas Live, including preservation of unsent edits when conflicts occur."},
			{"Create and attach assignment rubrics", "Verified in Canvas Live. Criterion maxima are preserved when ratings are omitted. New rubrics are attached independently of grade calculation. Local fixes on 2026-10-11 reject use_for_grading true on newly authored rubrics and explain independent grading in review; existing coupled snapshots remain supported. These fixes have local checks, not a new Canvas Live trial."},
			{"Attach a rubric to a New Quiz (ECR/SCR)", "Verified in Canvas Live through cse (CS8, 2026-10-10): pull-item and push attached the exact two-criterion independent rubric to New Quiz 3698192 while preserving points and settings. Other New Quiz edits through pull-item are refused. Written-work scoring uses the rubric as a comment-only scoring basis and writes no rubric assessment or quiz/item grade; the teacher enters item points in SpeedGrader."},
			{"Read Canvas data no command covers (cse api)", "Verified in Canvas Live (2026-10-10, courses 102279 and 102278): course metadata, modules/items, assignments, file metadata, Classic Quiz questions/answers, and New Quiz items/scoring data. A read-only Canvas API GET, one page per call, prints Canvas's JSON or error message and cannot write; error handling has local tests. Full archival, general binary downloads and vendor access are separate capabilities. When a write is needed, the agent gives the teacher the steps in Canvas and logs the gap in context/engine-notes.md for development."},
			{"Place newly created assignments in existing modules", "Verified in Canvas Live, including repeat handling without duplicates."},
			{"Pull text submissions and prior attempts", "Verified in Canvas Live with the built-in Test Student. A teacher-provided cloud Claude MCP run on 2026-10-11 also pulled ordinary CS8 student text and prior attempts; grade posting, completion and resubmission through that route remain unchecked. Dev, 2026-10-21: images embedded in the assignment directions are downloaded beside the packet (`direction_images`) so the agent can read a reference image; checked with a fake Canvas only, no Canvas Live run yet. Dev, 2026-10-21 (local tests): packets carry readable directions and student files carry readable_text only; the original HTML moves to side files (directions_html, body_html_path). Readable text now keeps code indentation, link addresses and image markers. Re-rendering this PC's 441 existing pulled files this way made packets 67% and student files 22% smaller; no Canvas Live pull with the new layout yet."},
			{"Author ungraded group discussions", "CS8 Canvas Live, 2026-10-17: distributed and direct-group topics, whole-thread child-source pulls and a teacher reply. Local checks cover course scope, explicit announcement intent, editable baselines and settings-only patches. Local fallback fixes reviewed 2026-10-19 retain recent_replies and incomplete reply-page coverage. Student views, attachment access and notifications remain unobserved."},
			{"Author graded discussions", "CS8 Canvas Live, 2026-10-17: a graded distributed discussion with an independent rubric, group set on the topic and an individual linked assignment; linked-topic rename synchronized the assignment. Local tests cover saved IDs, rubric-failure publication holds and resume. Direct-group topics and announcements cannot be graded. Discussion scoring is implemented separately; its Canvas Live observation, checkpoints and student views remain pending."},
			{"Assess graded discussion work individually", "Implemented slice 07; reviewed 2026-10-19. Per-student results use attributed own-post digests and cited context, with topic/link, changed-post and checkpoint guards. Local regressions now retain fallback preview replies and require complete relevant source coverage at pull and post before assessing missing work, allowing an independently complete club to proceed. Comments stay individual. Canvas Live, 2026-10-21 (PAP ELA7 3705186, Dev build 236a20f): one session pulled, scored and posted one ungraded entry; grade and comment succeeded and late status came back preserved because Canvas already held it. Checkpoints and student rendering remain unobserved."},
			{"Group work verified in Canvas Live", "Live check, 2026-10-17 on CS8 (course 121046) with the dev Engine, disposable `[CSE 1.1b DISPOSABLE]` objects only, all deleted afterwards: group set and club create/read/pull/update; membership add, move and remove for two students; a member-editable group Page create, pull, edit, unpublish and revision history; ungraded distributed and direct-group discussions, a graded distributed discussion with rubric whose group set stayed on the topic while the linked assignment stayed individual, linked-topic rename syncing the assignment, whole-thread pull with child sources, and a teacher reply; a module with a SubHeader, Discussion and ExternalUrl; a group assignment with group overrides, visibility restricted to the club, and date edits; a real shared submission pull (status ready, one artifact, two members, complete audience, new attempts tracked); a shared grade and rubric that reached both members once, group and private comments with the right audience and no replay on rerun, plus a shared late timing write; an individual-mode assignment with different grades, rubrics and private comments per student; and the local review page rendering group and private cards. Not yet observed: self sign-up and allocation, graded-discussion scoring (needs a student's own post), checkpointed discussions, excused or hidden members, student views and notifications."},
			{"Pull shared group assignment submissions", "CS8 Canvas Live, 2026-10-17: a real shared submission pull returned one artifact, two members, a complete audience and newly tracked attempts. Local checks cover selected-group scope, exact course/set identity, source-linked per-member evidence, placeholders, attachment deduplication and unsent results. Different artifacts or incomplete evidence can hold shared assessment while individual evidence remains usable. Excused/hidden members and student views remain unobserved."},
			{"Post shared group grades and feedback", "CS8 Canvas Live, 2026-10-17: one representative grade/rubric reached both members, with group and private comments scoped correctly and no replay, plus a shared late timing write. Local tests cover audience/attempt guards, coupled order, skip keys and private text. Local fixes reviewed 2026-10-19 require every reviewed member to match before reconciling uncertain shared late-only timing; prepared school-time/member provenance has a normal-suite preparation-to-post check. The calendar-backed correction path, excused/hidden members and student views remain pending live observation."},
			{"Post individual grades on a shared group product", "CS8 Canvas Live, 2026-10-17: different per-student grades, rubrics and private comments. Local fixes reviewed 2026-10-19 renew live assignment mode/basis and target group/attempt/artifact immediately before each numeric or rubric stage, holding remaining writes after a switch to shared grading while retaining accepted outcomes. Comment-only recovery reconciles original attempt-scoped text without blind repeats. Separate student review cards and optional shared feedback remain supported. Per-student late timing, student views and notifications remain unobserved."},
			{"Download file submissions and expose readable text", "A synthetic text-file submission was verified in Canvas Live."},
			{"Calculate component scores, unequal weights, and rubric-to-assignment scaling", "Exact arithmetic verified, including different rubric and assignment scales."},
			{"Grade assignments without a Canvas rubric", "An explicit local scoring basis works. Posts the grade and feedback without creating a rubric."},
			{"Post honest grades, rubric assessments, and feedback", "Canvas Live: earlier assignment grading runs posted honest grades and feedback, including replacing an existing higher grade. SCR 4, 5 and 6 were posted through the review page on 2026-10-11 in CS8 with real students; SCR 4 was confirmed present in Canvas, while SCR 5 and 6 were deliberately not re-read. The current rule that an accepted write counts as done, without post-write readback or reply-shape confirmation, has local tests only; the new MCP post path is pending checklist validation."},
			{"Feedback layout: overall, items, late marker and exemplar follow-up", "Verified in Canvas Live (CS8, 2026-10-17, disposable assignment 3703744 visible only to the built-in Test Student, then deleted): the default comment led with Overall: 16/20 (late) and one line per item, and the grade posted as 16. Follow-ups now use comment-only, which works on ordinary assignments and writes no grade: on a second disposable assignment (3703757, also deleted) a real lateness write recorded late with Canvas deducting 2 of the earned 16, the grade was then changed to 18 in Canvas, and the exemplar follow-up added only its comment, leaving 18. New Quiz comments never get an overall line (local tests). Exemplar selection across courses is playbook judgment, not yet used with real classes."},
			{"Post correctly when Canvas automatically grades from the rubric", "Earlier Canvas Live evidence verified the honest rubric assessment followed by the computed grade. The current accepted-write behavior has local tests only; a fresh live check of both independent and coupled rubric paths through MCP remains pending."},
			{"Revise a selected feedback comment without changing the grade", "Exact comment revision verified in Canvas Live, without a duplicate comment."},
			{"Apply supplied lateness timing and let Canvas calculate deductions", "Verified in Canvas Live. A changed due date holds the timing update while grading continues. On 2026-10-18 a disposable CS8 assignment visible only to the built-in Test Student (due date in the past, Test Student submission) was marked late by Canvas, and the Engine pull reported it as late. The CE-SE timing write itself was not exercised."},
			{"Create New Quizzes from QuizForge files", "Verified in Canvas Live (CS8, 2026-10-09): the original QuizForge all-types sampler (multiple choice, multiple answer, true/false, matching, fill-in-the-blank, numeric, ordering, categorization, with a stimulus passage and rationales) created one unpublished New Quiz through the New Quizzes API; reading it back showed every item type, authored points, feedback, and the student-visible result settings. A separate quiz verified time limit, attempts, due date, publication, and module placement. A resumed push completed without duplicating. Code blocks render in a dark Monokai box with Python colors and TEKS codes appear as a small label, both confirmed in the stored quiz. Local image import is not handled; authored Canvas file image HTML uses the explicit content path and needs its own access/rendering checks. Written items: see the New Quiz written items entry below. A teacher-provided 2026-10-11 cloud Claude MCP run also created and read back an unpublished MC/TF/ESSAY quiz. That run exposed ignored inline rationales. Local fixes on 2026-10-11 add the embedded QuizForge contract/example, warn on unknown item/choice keys, reject inline rationales with a correction hint, validate effective settings, and show canonical rationales in review. Quiz publication now follows successful requested module placement. Focused local checks cover these fixes; no new Canvas Live feedback readback or publication-failure trial is claimed."},
			{"Differentiated hub: restricted tier pages linked from an assignment or quiz", "Verified in Canvas Live (CS8, 2026-10-09) for assignment hub pages, reading state back from Canvas: each tier page is created unpublished, restricted to overrides, assigned to the matching non-collaborative tag, and only then published; a title collision stops the push before any write; an interrupted push resumes without duplicate pages; links in the hub description point at the exact page slugs. Hub is the only style offered (the Bridge was declined). Tiers can be added only when creating. Hub also works on New Quizzes (2026-10-10): pages are delivered unpublished, links are bound into the New Quiz instructions, and pages publish only with the quiz. Local tests cover the New Quiz path and a missing tag (page restricted to nobody, with a teacher action); no Canvas Live run of the New Quiz path or the missing-tag case is recorded. Not yet checked: what a student in each tier sees."},
			{"Recover interrupted work, avoid duplicate writes, and continue independent students", "Supported by live repeat and recovery checks plus focused local tests. Independent-student continuation was checked locally."},
		},
	},
	{
		Title: "Partial or awaiting meaningful validation", Status: capabilityYellow,
		Summary: "This group includes implemented features awaiting validation and features with partial support. Each entry states its limits and remaining checks; pending evidence alone does not prevent supported use.",
		Items: []capability{
			{"Timing and parent-report limits found in review", "Fixed locally, reviewed 2026-10-19: shared late-only completion requires all reviewed members; timing history finds valid local result contents including YAML, text, JSON-named and extensionless files outside courses; explicit null posting timestamps withhold parent feedback independently of grade fields. Awaiting-grading inventory and corrections availability are retained. The original failure evidence and dated resolutions are in docs/REVIEW-2026-10-19.md. No new Canvas Live, family delivery or UserInstall/UserSync adoption is claimed."},
			{"Calendar-backed late timing and late-only operations", "Reviewed 2026-10-21: the calendar supports non-school dates/ranges and school-time counting; grading periods remain relevant to parent reports, not the targeted scoring-session discovery design. `prepare_late_timing` checks first-genuine attempts and accommodation choices and returns proposed/unchanged/held actions without writing. Prepare timing only for work a session scores; already-scored work is not re-read or re-timed in a session. New individual and group packets include the saved private Extra time fact as true/false through stable identity and the active teacher-setup authority; older absent values remain unknown. The playbooks resolve only documented allowances, avoid applying an extension already in Canvas twice and hold only timing when the allowance is missing. The flag supplies no duration. Local regressions cover projection, old-packet compatibility, weekend/holiday seconds and preserved Canvas due-date guards. The 2026-10-19 fixes add whole-member shared recovery, preparation-to-post provenance and content-based local result discovery. `late-only` review/post changes timing fields without grades or feedback. Local tests cover timing; no new Canvas Live timing write is claimed. The 2026-10-21 read-only CS8 assignment-list observation is recorded with scoring-session discovery above. Scoped live timing and destination-client adoption remain pending."},
			{"Current-period parent report inventory", "Implemented and reviewed 2026-10-18: reports select the calendar period automatically, save timezone/date scope, inventory required work due in the clipped 14-day window and require visibility evidence. Missing/0, Corrections and History are scoped to that inventory; email and print include every inventory row. Explicitly unreleased grades remain listed without score/history/feedback. The 2026-10-19 fix withholds feedback for explicit posted_at null even when grade fields are null, keeping the honest awaiting-grading inventory status. Empty windows are a skip, and legacy scope-free runs are preserved but rejected for send/print. The explicit-null student due-date fallback defect is fixed: completion/classification regressions cover null and empty dates, malformed-date unavailability, omitted-date fallback and individualized dates. The local UserInstall and effective UserSync playbooks were updated on 2026-10-18. The running adapter still needs a reconnect; new behavior has no Canvas Live or family-delivery verification."},
			{"Group-work limits found in follow-up review", "Fixed locally, reviewed 2026-10-19: per-action individual group mode checks; uncertain comment-only no-replay and original-text reconciliation; fallback recent_replies; relevant fresh discussion coverage; placeholder-aware structural edits across pages; and changed-field-only group-set patches with explicit clears. These six failures and acceptance controls are in the normal test suite. The seed now includes delivered graded discussions, shared-only readiness and separate individual cards. See dated resolutions in docs/group-work/REVIEW-2026-10-17-followup.md. Earlier CS8 live observations retain their recorded scope."},
			{"CanvasExpert WebUI desktop shortcut", "Added 2026-10-16: ordinary install and WebUI app-connection setup create a shortcut on the current user's actual Windows desktop, targeting this UserInstall's webui.cmd. Repeat setup reuses the shortcut for the same target; a same-named shortcut for another target is preserved with a warning. Shortcut failure does not stop app registration or local checks, and webui.cmd remains available. Read-only inspection and check-only runs create no shortcut. Local Windows tests write and reload shortcuts in temporary folders with spaces and non-English names, with PATH empty, and verify target and working-directory file identity, repeat handling and conflict preservation, including equivalent Windows short and long paths. CLI/WebUI fixtures verify read-only modes and continuation after a shortcut warning. GitHub Windows CI for commit eed55bc passed tests, vet, packaging and the compiled MCP check on 2026-10-16. An installed-teacher desktop launch and district-PC behavior remain pending."},
			{"Home page commands", "Added 2026-10-16: Home leads with command cards (scoring session, planning session, quiz, parent update, Canvas fix) and a course picker that fills a one-sentence prompt for the teacher to copy into their teaching app. Commands come from teacher context/commands.md (UserInstall or UserSync); the agent edits it on request, and a missing or invalid file falls back to the seed with a note. Canvas and UserSync status moved to a compact strip; full controls stay under Settings → Connections. Local Go fixtures cover seed, teacher-edited and invalid command files. Nothing is sent to an agent or Canvas from Home; teacher acceptance remains pending."},
			{"Light/Dark WebUI appearance", "Implemented and reviewed 2026-10-16: Studio light styling, the existing dark palette, and an accessible switch that remembers an explicit choice in the active teacher-setup authority. Unset follows the OS. Local Go fixtures cover shared UserSync routing, isolated authenticated saves and standalone/terminal pages. Synthetic Edge browser checks cover OS changes and explicit overrides, new ports, unsaved settings/contact/review state, save failure, keyboard switching, and desktop/375px/320px layouts without JS or CSP errors. Teacher acceptance and actual provider delivery remain pending; this is local evidence, not Canvas Live proof."},
			{"Native Windows UserSync folder chooser", "Updated 2026-10-15: Browse calls the Windows Shell directly, removing its PowerShell/PATH and .NET dependency. An opt-in native test with PATH empty selected a temporary Unicode folder with spaces, canceled a selection, and closed on request cancellation. No admin access or extra runtime is required. Teacher confirmation from the installed Hub remains pending; paste-path fallback is retained."},
			{"Portable startup without PATH changes", "Reviewed 2026-10-15: packaged launchers and MCP connections use explicit Engine paths; no CE-SE PATH entry or developer runtime is required. Dev registration helper now invokes the selected Engine directly, and the Claude Explorer fallback uses the Windows directory API. Local empty-PATH fixtures check these mechanics; real client adoption remains pending. Moving UserInstall requires reconnecting the apps to its new path."},
			{"Restrictive district Windows 11", "Forecast reviewed 2026-10-15, not district validation: current Engine and MCP launcher are unsigned. Application/script allowlists, protected-folder writes and local agent/extension permissions can prevent setup despite no-admin and empty-PATH operation. Canvas transport uses platform TLS trust and environment proxies, with no Windows automatic-proxy/PAC integration. Loopback browser access, credential storage and Canvas token permissions await observation on the actual district PC. See docs/engine-capabilities.md."},
			{"Dev Hub launcher", "Updated 2026-10-15: webui.cmd uses Windows PowerShell at its standard absolute Windows path. A local copied-launcher fixture reached a synthetic script with PATH empty in a folder with spaces (exit 0); the actual Dev script help invocation also exited 0. Full Hub startup was not checked by this test. Packaged UserInstall launches the Engine directly."},
			{"Family Contact", "Reviewed 2026-10-20: free-form contact.json runs reuse the private family review, per-student Outlook messages and saved schema-2 outcomes. Course/group/ref audiences, Markdown or HTML, local inline images and attachments, parents-only routing and the saved closing are supported. Preparation reports duplicate matches, empty groups and unmatched students; changed contact or membership holds sending for a fresh preparation. The teacher alone chooses Send or Drafts only. Grade-update guarantees remain unchanged. Local checks passed 2026-10-20: full Go suite, vet, compiled 40-tool MCP smoke, and synthetic browser inline-image loading and skips. These establish Engine/browser behavior only. Local classic Outlook with a configured profile is required, with no computer-name restriction. Local Outlook draft check passed 2026-10-20: Engine SaveDraft saved a synthetic item to the configured profile, and saved-item inspection verified matching CID HTML and image/png MIME. Actual classic Outlook screenshot/accessibility inspection confirmed a visible blue-book image inline and schedule.txt in the attachment bar. Omitting the attachment Position argument keeps ordinary files visible. Outlook may normalize hidden-image metadata after opening. No Send was called and no real-family data was used. Cloud synchronization, other clients, authorized inbox delivery and installed-client adoption remain unobserved. No separate district-PC gate applies. No new Canvas Live or real-family send is claimed."},
			{"Parent updates by Outlook", "Reviewed 2026-10-17: the report read, drafts, a private review page showing each family's real recipients, and one Outlook email per student, with the student in To and enabled parents in CC, saved outcomes and no repeat sends (local tests; an Outlook draft with a CC line saved on the Dev PC). Canvas Live, read-only, 2026-10-16: the CS8 report read all 28 students with Canvas course scores; grade history now takes first scores from Canvas gradebook history, which showed a same-attempt regrade (0, then 80) that submission history hides. A one-student review page rendered the email from the report and held the student with no enabled parent email. A Go send to the profile's own address worked on the Dev PC. Changed for 1.1.0-beta.1 (local regressions): a positive teacher-entered grade resolves stale missing/no-submission indicators without a conflict hold; a current recorded zero goes first under Missing/0 regardless of submission, grading status or correction-window age, without implying it was unsubmitted. Missing/0 never repeats under Corrections; grade history remains. The Engine computes skip_eligible after normalization, including on run load: every included course must meet configured skip_score (90 by default), with no Missing/0 items. The report window and correction deadline come from `correction_days` in context/parent-updates.md (14 by default, 1 to 60; local tests only). Playbook/context seeds retain these standing rules and preserve teacher customization during updates. Earlier local changes make corrections available once work is finished and use the teacher's own portal/tutoring links. Pending: Canvas Live observation of these classifications, an email sent from the page, inbox arrival, the district PC, and an agent app driving the page."},
			{"Printable student reports", "Added 2026-10-16: from the same parent-update run, the Engine saves one PDF in the teacher's Downloads folder, one page per student, sorted by name and written to the student, and opens it. Microsoft Edge renders the PDF headless with a throwaway profile; if it cannot, a printable HTML file is saved instead. Every student gets a sheet; all missing, due-soon and grade-history items come from the report, and only corrections follow the agent's draft. Titles are plain text for paper, and no addresses or teacher-only notes appear. Local tests cover the sheets and page breaks; a CS8 dry run on the Dev PC produced a 28-page PDF. Printing on paper and Edge on the district PC are pending."},
			{"Private student and parent contact setup", "Added 2026-10-16 with local tests: Students separates Privacy Alias from editable Goes By, which starts with the Canvas first name, persists across roster refreshes, and addresses students in feedback without entering pseudonymized agent packets. Existing student CSV schemas remain compatible. Implemented 2026-10-15: one student email, repeatable parent phone/email entries and independent text/email Yes/No choices; US phone formatting, optional destinations and private JSON excluded from agent file tools. Reusable setup (course selections, student aliases/settings/notes and contacts) follows configured UserSync; grading/planning session files and machine credentials stay local. Local fixtures cover preservation and two-UserInstall restoration. Synthetic browser checks cover contact rows, independent radios, formatting and draft restoration. Real provider delivery and teacher browser validation remain pending. Email delivery is covered above; texting remains unimplemented."},
			{"Automatic Canvas connection check in Home and Connections", "Implemented 2026-10-12: Home and Connections show cached Checking, Connected, Token rejected, Unavailable or Not connected status. The check is one bounded authenticated read-only Canvas identity request per saved token; manual Test retries it. Focused local mocks cover success, authentication rejection, network failure, missing credentials, navigation during a blocked request, and ignoring results after credential replacement/removal. A temporary fake-credential browser fixture confirmed the displayed states and navigation. Updated 2026-10-13: Unavailable now separates a Canvas response (with its status) from no response or a timeout and never advises replacing the token; a local test covers the wording. On 2026-10-13 one hub run against a temporary UserInstall used this machine's saved credential: the read-only identity request showed Connected (Canvas Live, read-only; no write). Rejected and unavailable states remain local-mock evidence."},
			{"Choose and test the saved teacher-rules UserSync folder", "Implemented 2026-10-12: Browse uses the native Windows folder chooser to populate a draft; only Use UserSync folder changes authority. Cancel and chooser failure retain the typed path, with paste as fallback. Test reads the saved configured directory and never writes, binds the draft, falls back to UserInstall or claims provider delivery. Local mocked chooser and temporary folder tests cover selection, cancellation, chooser failure, nonblocking navigation, available/unavailable status, no writes, explicit save and return to UserInstall. Browser inspection used temporary UserInstall/UserSync roots: the native chooser opened and returned a candidate, which stayed unbound; chooser cancellation was verified with the mock. The temporary saved folder tested as Available. Provider delivery remains unobserved."},
			{"Set up an agent connection", "Guidance reviewed 2026-10-15: Set this all up covers app connections, Canvas, saved courses, optional shared setup and intended-assistant verification, preserving completed steps and waiting only for necessary teacher input. The install command remains compatible; real first-run agent adoption remains pending. Earlier evidence reviewed 2026-10-13: the ZIP has a selected-client helper, Work registration with configuration preservation, and a thin Cowork extension targeting UserInstall's Engine. Local package/MCP checks passed on 2026-10-12. A fresh Windows laptop pilot on the recorded development build saved Work settings, prepared Cowork and passed local checks, but both automatic WebUI starts timed out. Dev repairs since that pilot (local tests only, not yet observed on a laptop): the installer WebUI start now shares the normal same-UserInstall lock/reuse path and reports a warning with a webui.cmd fallback on failure; Claude extension setup tries a direct app launch with the file, then reveals it in File Explorer with manual steps; mismatch messages name both Canvas origins; the Canvas address field accepts bare hosts or pasted HTTPS links; setup wording asks Claude, ChatGPT, or both (since replaced by automatic detection, below). The laptop cause of the missing starter origin was not reproduced locally and remains unconfirmed. The root install-log.jsonl records sanitized outcomes outside private state and UserSync. Cowork trust/install completion and real tool calls in both destinations remain pending; verify the intended UserInstall root and actual saved courses after reconnect. Added later, local fixture tests only: Google Antigravity registration (JSON merge with backup), and a default install that connects every detected app (Claude, ChatGPT, Antigravity) instead of asking; no real app has been observed adopting an Antigravity entry. See docs/engine-capabilities.md and handoffs/retired/FRESH-INSTALL-TRIAGE-20261013.md."},
			{"Use reusable teacher setup across PCs", "Reviewed 2026-10-16: configured UserSync is the shared authority for teacher rules/preferences, course configuration, student aliases/settings/notes, and private roster/contact records. Grading/planning sessions, course work and Engine stay in UserInstall; credentials stay on each machine. Without UserSync, all setup stays in UserInstall. Local temporary UserInstall/UserSync fixtures cover direct shared authority, preserved custom rules/local originals, bootstraps, active seed addition/replacement archives, current reads and stale-hash rejection. Settings grading voice, CLI rules-location, CLI playbooks status/replace and MCP engine_info use the same per-UserInstall binding; selected replacement requires a current hash (or an explicit missing-file precondition) and archives the active copy. An integrated extracted-package fixture with a path containing spaces bound a synthetic OneDrive - Test District/Teacher Rules path and explicitly adopted AGENTS.md with its prior copy archived. Unavailable UserSync reports its path without stale-copy fallback. Actual cloud-provider delivery and human-client adoption remain pending observation; no live UserInstall or Canvas migration was performed. See docs/engine-capabilities.md."},
			{"Local MCP adapter for agent connections", "Implemented: 37 typed tools. Pinned Go 1.27.1 packaged build and `node scripts/check-mcp.mjs dist/cse.exe` passed on 2026-10-17, including compiled stdio discovery and validation of the group/Page/discussion adapters. The extracted packaged Engine, invoked from another working directory, returned three synthetic saved courses and the correct UserInstall root. Doctor offline JSON skipped Canvas/hub requests; this machine's existing credential origin differed from the synthetic course origin, so doctor reported that mismatch and exited 4 without a Canvas request. Local doctor reports Engine/build identity, UserInstall and active-rule readability, course configuration, saved-origin consistency and a temporary native dummy credential round trip, plus a bounded authenticated read-only Canvas identity check and same-UserInstall hub identity probe. Canvas account identity and response bodies are discarded; authentication rejection is distinct from network/DNS/TLS/service errors. Focused mocks cover authenticated success/rejection/network failure and offline no-call behavior; synthetic hub fixtures cover healthy/stale/absent discovery. These results do not establish that a browser page appeared or a destination client adopted MCP. Destination reconnect and use of the new build remain pending. Current review/posting, New Quiz pull and file-download workflows through MCP remain unverified. See docs/new-quiz-written-work-spec.md and docs/mcp-adapter.md."},
			{"Dev, UserInstall, UserSync and MCP configuration", "Reviewed 2026-10-15: Dev produces the user ZIP in dist/. The extracted folder is already UserInstall and runs in place; setup connects apps and Canvas without creating a second product folder. Optional UserSync holds reusable teacher setup (including course selections and student settings/notes/contacts), synchronized by its provider; grading/planning sessions stay in UserInstall. CLI/API/storage spellings remain compatible. The packaged cse.cmd resolved the extracted UserInstall from another working directory despite spaces in its path. Packaged webui.cmd started the synthetic UserInstall's local hub; its second invocation reported same-UserInstall reuse and the identity route returned that UserInstall root. A browser launch was requested, not visually confirmed. New Cowork bundles forward stdio through a thin launcher to UserInstall's Engine; replacing an old extension requires the client's trust/install action. Work registration respects configured Codex home and preserves unrelated client settings. Local package fixtures verify these mechanics, not destination adoption or Canvas Live behavior. Existing teacher files and unsent work are preserved."},
			{"Keep teacher choices across updates", "Added 2026-10-17 (local tests and a local ZIP run, no teacher install yet): the ZIP no longer carries playbooks, TEACHER.md, Teacher_Override.md or context/, so extracting a new version over a folder cannot overwrite the teacher's setup. On first run the bundled Engine lays them down; cse playbooks update (MCP update-playbooks) replaces only playbooks still identical to the previous shipped copy, keeps teacher-edited ones for agent reconciliation, keeps each shipped version under shipped/, and never touches context/ or Teacher_Override.md. A local run extracted the ZIP, added an override, a portal name and a playbook edit, extracted the ZIP over the folder again, and all three survived; update reported the edited playbook as kept. The teacher's own sync-mode UserInstall was updated 2026-10-17: nine older unedited files were adopted, teacher settings were untouched, the UserSync pointer files are restored by update, and Claude loaded the new Engine after a restart. Update now recognizes unedited copies of any past shipped version from embedded fingerprints and ignores line-ending-only differences. A reconciliation check on that install kept a test teacher edit through a changed shipped playbook with a clean three-way merge, then the test edits were removed. A colleague's update and background reconciliation by an agent remain pending."},
			{"New Quiz written items (essay, file upload) in push-quiz", "Added 2026-10-10: push-quiz creates ESSAY and FILEUPLOAD items with optional word limits and accepted file types. Canvas Live API storage evidence (CS8, 2026-10-10) confirmed items, points and settings were stored as sent; student-visible limit enforcement remains pending human Build/Preview validation. Separately, Canvas Live Student Analysis returned a typed answer for one student on CS8 quiz 3698192 (2026-10-11); one uploaded DOCX was downloaded byte-exact in a teacher-authorized hand-run. The Engine now has a New Quiz pull path for typed responses and file downloads, with local tests only. MCP validation on the current runtime and a fresh Canvas Live Engine pull remain pending; New Quiz comments never write grades. See docs/new-quiz-written-work-spec.md."},
			{"Score New Quiz written work (ECR/SCR)", "Available for regular teacher use within supported limits: explicitly scoped pull reads typed responses and downloads files; comment-only results use review/post to send truthful criterion scores and feedback without an aggregate quiz assessment (a 2026-10-17 local fix stopped the default comment header from adding a whole-quiz Assessment line; local tests only). This path cannot write grades, rubric assessments or late timing; the teacher enters per-item points in SpeedGrader. Dev now suppresses a current-attempt comment already posted from session pulls while Canvas still awaits written-item points, and reports the student count for a SpeedGrader reminder. Focused fixtures cover that suppression and a new attempt's return. Canvas Live, 2026-10-21: one agent-run scoring session on Dev build 236a20f under the teacher's scope (ELA7, PAP ELA7, CS8; direct post) pulled 24 students in 5 packets in about 50 s. New Quiz students with a CE-SE comment on the current attempt were not pulled again and were reported as 'comment posted, item points not entered'; for all 7 assignments Canvas needs-grading equalled pulled plus comment-posted (agent report, counts read once). The saved results files show two New Quiz comment-only posts (PAP 3705775, 3705779) and one graded-discussion grade and comment (PAP 3705186) succeeded. Needs-grading counts before and after a comment were not compared. Current live Engine/MCP report, file and comment paths remain unverified. Separate Canvas Live hand-runs (CS8 quiz 3698192, 2026-10-11, one student) read typed work, downloaded one DOCX byte-exact and posted one comment. Evidence gaps are not a blanket prohibition on supported use. See docs/new-quiz-written-work-spec.md."},
			{"Author standalone Pages and rich assignment directions", "Added 2026-10-10: push accepts Page create/update documents and pull-page preserves exact live HTML with a baseline; optional existing module placement finishes before requested publication. Explicit HTML bodies support authored tables, code, images and file links; assignment creation defaults to the existing Markdown subset. Raw HTML assignment review uses escaped source. Local tests cover identity, resumption and conflict preservation. No live Engine Page authoring or rich assignment-create trial is recorded; saved HTML normalization and browser/student appearance still need validation. Restricted hub delivery remains separate."},
			{"Upload course assets with reusable receipts", "Added 2026-10-10: upload-file uses course upload initiation, multipart transfer and completion, with rename collisions and explicit course/hidden/locked access. Returned IDs, source hashes and stable references persist; unchanged receipts verify/reuse files and changed bytes require a deliberate new upload. Locked access requires an existing locked course folder; hidden files remain accessible through links. Local transport tests cover credential isolation and resumption. No live Engine course upload, video player or caption/student-access trial is recorded."},
			{"Assemble native modules from existing content", "CS8 dev Engine, 2026-10-17: a module with SubHeader, Discussion and ExternalUrl items. Local tests cover ordered Page/File/Assignment/Discussion/ExternalUrl/SubHeader placement, same-course group URL guards, saved destination-aware resume and scoped collaboration/conference metadata reads. Module links grant no group access or publication. Student visibility, external provider access and standalone course Page behavior remain pending; provider provisioning and content reads are separate."},
			{"Review scores on a local page before posting (cse review)", "Canvas Live evidence (CS8, 2026-10-10, disposable assignment 3698181, built-in Test Student): the review page was used to revise, re-review and post; grade and comment were read back. Local tests cover the current per-student cards, including submission text and attachment names above feedback. A temporary synthetic browser fixture inspected ordinary and comment-only review pages, evidence, private notes, controls and completion/error outcomes in light/dark desktop/mobile layouts; no Canvas write occurred. The compiled Engine passed a synthetic MCP review check: the page served, a synthetic revision was submitted, and review_status returned the saved revision. Review pages are temporary and stop serving after the review finishes; reopening a left-open tab afterward will show a connection error. Current installed-client review behavior, multi-student scoring/posting and student rendering remain pending human validation."},
			{"Change New Quiz question points (cse quiz-points)", "Added 2026-10-10: lists a New Quiz's questions, or sets the points of the questions named by position, then reads them back; works on quizzes made in Canvas too. Writes once students have submitted but warns that Canvas may not regrade existing attempts (check the gradebook; the quiz editor offers regrade) and reports when the items' total differs from the quiz total. Local tests, plus a Canvas Live listing of quiz 3698192; the item points write itself matches the one-off call that set that quiz's items to 50 earlier the same day."},
			{"Read PDF, Word, image, and other non-text attachment contents", "Original files are preserved. Built-in readable extraction currently handles text formats; other formats need additional reading tools."},
			{"Discover unfinished work, skip completed attempts, and find resubmissions", "Targeted scoring-session discovery is implemented in Dev. Read-only Canvas Live observation on CS8 (2026-10-21) directly confirmed `needs_grading_count` on assignment-list results: 30 assignments returned and all 30 had the field; examples included 3698355 count 1, 3703860 count 20, and 3697517 count 0. A follow-up detailed read for 3698355 returned one current submitted/ungraded attempt (attempt 1, submitted 2026-10-21T14:47:45Z); the earlier two-row timing packet was timestamped 2026-10-21T13:31:09.480035Z, before that submission, reconciling the apparent count mismatch. No student identities are recorded. This verifies the field and reconciles the count. On 2026-10-21 the Dev Engine also ran one read-only `pull-work --session` on CS8 into a scratch workspace: of 30 assignments, 28 collapsed into the summary line; 3698355 pulled 1 student (1 timing candidate, 22 already scored) and 3703860, not yet due, pulled 20. Discovery used 5 requests (about 5s). With attachment downloads run concurrently at the client's 4-request cap, fetch took 5.6s and 86 requests for 21 attachments, against 19.8s when they ran serially, with no failed downloads. No Canvas write occurred and no New Quiz was pulled. This is a live read-only run of discovery and packet production, not a scoring or posting session. Passing local fixtures cover zero-count skip, absent-count fallback, not-yet-due inclusion, avoiding per-student fetches and already-scored rereads, concurrent attachment downloads, comment-only completion with new-attempt return, closed-period skip, no calendar-period prerequisite and indexed result lookup. The full local suite and vet pass. Canvas Live, 2026-10-21: one agent-run scoring session on Dev build 236a20f under the teacher's scope (ELA7, PAP ELA7, CS8; direct post) pulled 24 students in 5 packets in about 50 s. New Quiz students with a CE-SE comment on the current attempt were not pulled again and were reported as 'comment posted, item points not entered'; for all 7 assignments Canvas needs-grading equalled pulled plus comment-posted (agent report, counts read once). The saved results files show two New Quiz comment-only posts (PAP 3705775, 3705779) and one graded-discussion grade and comment (PAP 3705186) succeeded. New Quiz counts before/after a comment, a resubmission, a group assignment through session discovery and a teacher spot-check of that session's grades remain pending live validation. Explicit assignment pulls retain reassessment behavior."},
			{"What Canvas keeps and shows in each field", "One reference, served to agents by cse help fields, records each field with its evidence level. Canvas Live API read-back (CS8, 2026-10-10, unpublished probe New Quiz 3698178 and assignment 3698180): the New Quiz kept realistic quiz HTML (headings, emphasis, lists, a table with colspan, inline styles, the code box, LaTeX text, the equation image, links) and removed only script and onclick; New Quizzes returned course images as expiring signed links; choices and feedback were stored exactly; matching text was stored raw, while ordering text had & and < escaped; assignment directions kept every heading level, bold, italic, code and both link kinds. Teacher views the same day: in New Quiz Preview the image, inline style, LaTeX (rendered as math), equation image, code box and choice formatting all displayed; matching text showed tags literally while ordering text rendered them, with & and < shown normally in both and line breaks collapsed to spaces; the assignment page showed every heading, bold, italic and the code block. Earlier views: in New Quiz teacher Preview the code box was dark and colored, matching/ordering text plain, and feedback appeared after submitting; a submission comment kept its line breaks in Student View. SpeedGrader display of submission-comment paragraphs is still unchecked. A 2026-10-10 page check went through the Canvas editor, so it is not Engine-path evidence."},
			{"Student experience of quizzes and hub pages", "Partially checked. Canvas cannot open a New Quiz as the built-in Test Student, so New Quizzes need the editor's Preview or a real enrolled account. Ordinary enrolled-student behavior and hub tier pages remain unverified from a student account. Read-back of authoring and restrictions does not establish those broader experiences."},
			{"Produce useful educational judgments and feedback in the teacher's voice", "Playbooks exist. Teaching quality and student-facing usability still need a human validation check; synthetic tests do not establish them."},
		},
	},
	{
		Title: "Future capabilities", Status: capabilityRed,
		Summary: "These are things we want CE-SE to do. The requested operations are not implemented yet.",
		Items: []capability{
			{"Manage book clubs and collaborative group work", "Tier A and B are implemented; reviewed 2026-10-19. The CS8 dev Engine check on 2026-10-17 exercised group sets/clubs, membership changes, Pages, ungraded and graded discussion authoring, whole-thread pulls/replies, module links, group assignments/dates, real shared submissions, shared and individual grades/rubrics/comments, shared timing and review cards. The seed playbook covers these delivered paths. Local regression fixes have no new live evidence. Self sign-up/allocation, checkpoints, excused/hidden members and student views/notifications remain pending. Tier C remains frozen until requested; external provider provisioning remains separate."},
			{"Set up peer reviews, group calendars, or conference sign-up", "No typed management or provisioning workflow is available. Slice 16 reads existing collaboration and conference metadata in a configured course or exact collaborative club, including safe returned links and known participant refs. It does not create Google/Microsoft documents or meetings, read provider content/recordings, or prove contribution/attendance. See docs/book-club-group-work-discovery.md for the research and remaining direction."},
			{"Add hub tiers to an existing assignment or quiz", "Hub pages are created together with a new assignment or New Quiz. Adding them to existing content, and the Bridge style (declined by design), are not available."},
			{"Apply individual extensions or accommodations to Canvas deadlines", "Reviewed 2026-10-18: writing individual Canvas deadlines is not implemented. The private Extra time checkbox now reaches individual/group scoring evidence; the playbooks use an established allowance through the existing accommodated-deadline timing preparation, preserving Canvas's effective date as the write guard. The flag supplies no duration and local settings do not change Canvas dates. Timing preparation/projection have local tests and the effective playbooks are installed in UserInstall; the running adapter needs a reconnect, and Canvas Live timing observation remains pending."},
			{"Import a QuizForge QTI ZIP", "Tried 2026-10-09 through Canvas content migration: it produced an empty New Quiz with no error, so it is not offered. QuizForge content would need conversion to the quiz file format."},
			{"Manage standalone/shared rubrics or edit existing rubric definitions", "Current support creates and attaches new rubrics to assignments and New Quizzes."},
			{"Synchronize or reorganize existing module structure", "Native module assembly adds only explicitly requested entries. Deletion, replacement, prerequisites and completion requirements are not implemented."},
			{"Write New Quiz item scores or per-item feedback", "Automatic New Quiz item-score and per-item feedback writes are not implemented. Supported written-work scoring posts criterion scores and feedback in a whole-assignment comment; the teacher enters item points in SpeedGrader. The comment-only operation also writes no quiz grade, rubric assessment or late timing."},
			{"Apply grading curves", "Future capability."},
		},
	},
}

func init() {
	register(page{Path: "/capabilities", Template: "capabilities", Scripts: []string{"appearance.js"},
		Nav:    []navSlot{{Primary: "Guide", Label: "Capabilities", Order: 42}},
		Handle: (*Hub).capabilitiesPage})
}

func (h *Hub) capabilitiesPage(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
	h.render(w, http.StatusOK, tmpl("capabilities"), struct {
		Appearance appearanceData
		Reviewed   string
		Groups     []capabilityGroup
	}{appearanceFor(h.root, h.secret), capabilitiesReviewed, capabilityGroups})
}
